Interpretation
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bare hole and gate tournaments are beautifully small but usually mixed:
  they forget where the observer clasp is.  This is the main hidden assumption.
Anchoring the observer cells/gates restores purity at the cost of label tax.
Hole-only tournaments are the most radical: vertices are vacancies, not
  runners or sectors.  They suggest an exclusion-process version of LRC.
Gate-priority tournaments are kinetic data structures: edges change exactly
  when boundary-crossing certificates fail.  LRC becomes a question about
  whether the two observer gates can jointly lose incoming pressure.
